The legal text comes from an official publication of Burkina Faso:

  Constitution du Burkina Faso, adoptée par le référendum du 02 juin 1991, révisée par les lois n°002/97/ADP,
  003-2000/AN, 001-2002/AN, 015-2009/AN, 023-2012/AN, 033-2012/AN, 035-2013/AN et 072-2015/CNT, as consolidated by
  the Assemblée nationale ("Constitution consolidée après la relecture du 05 nov 2015") and published on
  LegiBurkina, the legal portal of the Secrétariat général du Gouvernement et du Conseil des ministres (SGG-CM/DSI),
  https://www.legiburkina.gov.bf/documents/b157d74c-23a1-4025-a8d6-0061e83df0c2/download
  (listed at https://www.legiburkina.gov.bf/textesFondamentaux), retrieved 29 October 2026.

The portal states "SGGCM/DSI @2025 - Tous droits réservés" for the site and no licence for the legal texts. They
are official legal texts; their copyright status is not confirmed here, and they are reproduced with the
attribution above.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; page numbers, footnotes and their markers, and the cover page were
removed; headings were gathered in one structure file; one paragraph printed on the same line as the end of the
previous one (art. 101) was put on its own line; and the text was arranged as git commits. The wording of the law
was not changed. Neither the Secrétariat général du Gouvernement nor the Assemblée nationale endorses this
repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
